stream
BT
/F1 24.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 684.00 Tm (The Art of Reading Deeply) Tj
/F1 12.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 665.00 Tm (A short field guide to reading less, but understanding more) Tj
/F1 11.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 630.50 Tm (Most of us were taught to read, but almost none of us were taught to read well. We move our) Tj
/F1 11.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 614.00 Tm (eyes across a page, reach the bottom, and call it done. Yet a week later the ideas have) Tj
/F1 11.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 597.50 Tm (quietly slipped away, like water through open fingers. Reading deeply is a different craft. It) Tj
/F1 11.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 581.00 Tm (is slower, more deliberate, and far more rewarding. This guide lays out four habits that turn) Tj
/F1 11.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 564.50 Tm (passive reading into something that actually sticks.) Tj
/F1 11.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 540.00 Tm (None of these habits require talent. They require intent. If you practice them on even a) Tj
/F1 11.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 523.50 Tm (single document, you will notice the difference immediately: the text stops washing over you) Tj
/F1 11.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 507.00 Tm (and starts talking back.) Tj
/F1 15.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 467.00 Tm (1. Read with a Pencil in Hand) Tj
/F1 11.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 442.50 Tm (The single greatest upgrade to your reading is to stop reading with your eyes alone and start) Tj
/F1 11.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 426.00 Tm (reading with your hands. Highlight the sentence that surprises you. Underline the claim you) Tj
/F1 11.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 409.50 Tm (disagree with. In the margin, write the question that the paragraph refuses to answer. A) Tj
/F1 11.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 393.00 Tm (marked-up page is a record of a conversation between you and the author.) Tj
/F1 11.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 368.50 Tm (Do not highlight everything; a page drowned in yellow is as useless as a blank one. Mark only) Tj
/F1 11.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 352.00 Tm (what earns it: the load-bearing idea, the surprising fact, the sentence you want to find again) Tj
/F1 11.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 335.50 Tm (in six months. The act of choosing what to highlight is itself the work of understanding.) Tj
/F1 15.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 295.50 Tm (2. Ask the Document Questions) Tj
/F1 11.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 271.00 Tm (A good reader interrogates the text. Before you begin, ask what you expect to learn. While) Tj
/F1 11.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 254.50 Tm (you read, ask whether the argument holds. When you finish, ask what you would say if the) Tj
/F1 11.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 238.00 Tm (author were sitting across the table. Questions convert a wall of prose into a set of problems) Tj
/F1 11.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 221.50 Tm (your mind wants to solve.) Tj
/F1 11.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 197.00 Tm (The best questions are often the naive ones. Why is this true? What would break if it were) Tj
/F1 11.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 180.50 Tm (false? Who does this leave out? A document that cannot survive honest questions was never) Tj
/F1 11.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 164.00 Tm (worth memorizing in the first place.) Tj
/F1 15.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 124.00 Tm (3. Turn Notes into Flashcards) Tj
/F1 11.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 99.50 Tm (Understanding fades; retrieval endures. The most reliable way to remember what you read is) Tj
/F1 11.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 83.00 Tm (to test yourself on it, spaced out over days and weeks. Take the ideas you highlighted and) Tj
ET
