/F1 11.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 703.50 Tm (phrase each as a question with a short answer. Then, instead of rereading, try to recall. The) Tj
/F1 11.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 687.00 Tm (struggle to remember is precisely what builds the memory.) Tj
/F1 11.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 662.50 Tm (This is called spaced repetition, and decades of research support it. A card reviewed just as) Tj
/F1 11.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 646.00 Tm (you are about to forget it is worth a dozen passive rereads. Five minutes of recall beats an) Tj
/F1 11.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 629.50 Tm (hour of highlighting you never revisit.) Tj
/F1 15.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 589.50 Tm (4. Teach It Back) Tj
/F1 11.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 565.00 Tm (You do not truly understand an idea until you can explain it to someone who does not. Close) Tj
/F1 11.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 548.50 Tm (the document and say the argument out loud in plain language. Wherever you stumble, you) Tj
/F1 11.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 532.00 Tm (have found the exact seam where your understanding is thin. Return to the page, repair the) Tj
/F1 11.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 515.50 Tm (gap, and try again.) Tj
/F1 11.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 491.00 Tm (Teaching back is the honest test. It refuses to let you mistake familiarity for knowledge. If) Tj
/F1 11.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 474.50 Tm (you can hand the idea to another person intact, it is finally yours.) Tj
/F1 11.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 440.00 Tm (Four habits, one theme: reading is not something you receive, it is something you do. Mark) Tj
/F1 11.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 423.50 Tm (the page, question it, test yourself, and teach it back. Do that, and the words stop being ink) Tj
/F1 11.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 72.00 407.00 Tm (on a page and become part of how you think.) Tj
ET
